# Git auth in Cursor agent shells

Cursor agent shells on this machine sometimes set `HOME=1356` (relative/invalid). That breaks:

- `git push` / `git pull` (cannot read GitHub creds from osxkeychain)
- `git commit` identity (falls back to `jondev@R2D2.local` instead of real `.gitconfig`)
- Homebrew and `~/.ssh`

**Before any git network or commit command, run:**

```bash
export HOME=/Users/jondev
```

Or prefix:

```bash
HOME=/Users/jondev git push
HOME=/Users/jondev git commit ...
```

Do not print credential helper output (tokens). If `1356/` appears in the repo root, delete it; it is junk from the bad HOME.
